        <updated>2025-08-09T05:26:14.000Z</updated>
        <content type="html"><![CDATA[<img src="https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/55398995?u=9f6a9837c9879eceb0abde487a338b92d4e206fc&v=4" width="64" height="64" alt=""/><br/><p dir="auto">After <a class="issue-link js-issue-link" data-error-text="Failed to load title" data-id="3207883044" data-permission-text="Title is private" data-url="https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/40228" data-hovercard-type="pull_request" data-hovercard-url="/mdn/content/pull/40228/hovercard" href="https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/40228">#40228</a>, we are a lot more explicit on some CSS stylistic decisions. In particular, we now have systematic rules surrounding the preferred color notations. In this batch of PRs, I'm converting all short hex to long hex. The benefit is: readers can more easily understand the syntax; there's one less syntactic variability; if I want to grep all occurrences of one hex color, I can do that more easily without <code class="notranslate">#aaa</code> also matching <code class="notranslate">#aaaddd<span class="ml-1 d-inline-block border circle color-border-subtle" style="background-color: #aaaddd; height: 8px; width: 8px;"></span></code>.</p>]]></content>
